> I assumed here the desire was to snapshot the creator document's referrer policy at new-document creation time.

That's what I would expect also.

@annevk @bzbarsky have you had a chance to look at this PR yet?

> The bit about "Otherwise (e.g., if the navigation was to a URL with a local scheme)" doesn't make sense to me either. If I navigate to a blob: is there not a response? In what actual situations is there no response? If I have a document with referrer policy A which creates a subframe, then a document with referrer policy B navigates that subframe to a blob:, is the referrer policy of the result A or B? It should be B. I think this spec proposal makes it A.

@annevk, could you help figuring this out? As I said in my OP, it might be that we need to clean up navigation around local schemes in general. But maybe I'm just doing it wrong in this patch.

@estark37, do you or any of your editors know the answer to my

> I did not understand the intent of https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-referrer-policy/#referrer-policy-delivery-implicit-workers.

?

I'd like to keep moving on this if we can.
